{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert the justice of a stranger, etc.</b> Meaning: lest you say, since HaShem has commanded me concerning the stranger, I shall tilt his judgment in his favor — Scripture therefore says, ״לֹא תַטֶּה״ etc. And He concludes, <b>nor shall you take a widow's garment in pledge</b> — meaning, only in this matter do I command you to tilt in her favor, that you shall not take a widow's garment in pledge other than at the time of the loan, even though in the case of all others besides her you may take their garments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:52.401198543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}